# tests/test_placement_regression_a107.mojo
# A-107: Placement regression battery -- the placement
# decision stack's verdicts on the standard fixture and
# scenario sets, pinned as full-tier tests.
#
# What is pinned, and why it is a battery rather than a
# repeat of the per-slice tests: A-100/A-102/A-103/A-104/
# A-105 each assert the properties of their own decisions
# (device class here, a bound there). This battery pins the
# COMPLETE rendered decision for every standard case --
# device, backend, reason text, measured estimate, A-099
# fallback, spill totals, re-plan audit lines, split
# accounting, fairness summaries and log digests -- so ANY
# future decision change, however small, fails loudly here
# until a numbers-backed slice re-pins it deliberately.
#
# Scope honesty: A-106 (scheduler telemetry) had not landed
# when this battery was pinned, so nothing here depends on
# it. The pins cover the banked decision stack only:
# A-100 planner (12 standard fixtures, plus the GPU-absent
# registry and the unproven-context variants), A-102
# spillover (6 standard plans), A-103 re-planning (the
# mixed generation script under GPU loss, NPU loss, CPU
# loss, and the seeded failure drill), A-104 big-model
# splits (6 named splits + the budget ladder), A-105
# fairness (5 standard demand scripts).
#
# Pin discipline: pins were generated by running the banked
# code (probe in hidden_files, A-107 ledger) and reviewed
# line by line against the per-slice tests' asserted
# expectations before being written here. Fake registries
# throughout, exactly as the A-100/A-103 suites build them:
# no live hardware is probed, so the battery is a pure
# function of the decision code and the measured tables it
# embeds. To change a pin: land the numbers-backed slice
# that justifies the new decision, regenerate, review the
# diff pin by pin, and say so in that slice's ledger.

